# PROVISIONAL Qwen3.8-Flash-Next TP2 candidate profile: the Phase 0 proving model (plans/PLAN.md) across two Sparks,
# with the architecture on. This is not a Qwen4 size and none of its numbers carry over to one. The engine is
# MiaAI-Lab's dual-Spark Flash-Next engine, forward-ported onto our engine base and selected with
# TF_FLASHNEXT_ENGINE=mia, plus our compute lane, the in-model runner and S3 (tool-full, as the TP1 candidate).
# Copy to profiles/provisional/qwen38-flash-next-tp2-mia-tool-full.env (git-ignored) on both nodes and fill in the
# node-local values. Rank 1 starts first on the second node, then rank 0 serves.
#
# Credit: the engine is Mia's (MiaAI-Lab), from her recipe
#   https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Dual-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold at dc05c912342ec19467b3b7b686888de763f2ada1
# (Apache License 2.0). Her patches 0001-0008 and 0010-0012 are in the engine branch as her own commits; her LICENSE,
# NOTICE and CREDITS ship in its LICENSES/ folder. Her patch 0009 (Python vision) is not ported: the port serves text.
# The serve settings below are hers (her start.sh and m2 config), with her --kv-dtype fp8 under our name --kv-cache.
PROFILE=qwen38-flash-next-tp2-mia-tool-full
RANKS=2
# The engine: qwen4/mia-tp2 at 188d9c63c23a (2026-11-11). That is 2f77d333d362 (her engine as flashnext_mia, our lane
# commits, and her lane scheduling as her family's defaults: burst admission, pooled shared budgets, head stops, her
# store's short-prompt rule; plus robust boot timing of every cost table and the compute lane's think-block fixes),
# then the forced-rows fix (c8e930375: a forced result's rows all land before any stream hold), then the runner in
# thinking chats only (1a7ed13bb, 2026-11-11: see TF_RUNNER_SPANS below), the two TP1 already runs.
# Then qwen4/mia-tp2-next at 4c4e966eb470 (2026-11-12): 188d9c63c23a plus a cut XML tool call's value dropping the
# closer it began (6f4cf8bc2, as TP1's 501674d7f), the fill picker finishing an open chunk before it switches
# (03ad01b69), lane costs kept between loads (bd4d23ccb, see COST_CACHE_DIR) and a per-rank load-stage log line.
# Then qwen4/mia-tp2-next-digitstop at d306dc2fe26e (2026-11-12): 4c4e966eb470 plus the tool_choice support
# (80c12fc12: required, named and any), the thinking-budget fix (d97058206: a budget cut inside a compute-lane result
# no longer fails the reply) and the runner's digit stop (no drawn digit right after an owned inline integer in
# reasoning, a 1024-digit reasoning run cap; TF_RUNNER_DIGIT_STOP / TF_RUNNER_DIGIT_RUN_MAX, on by default).
# Build its runner image: the native image (tensorfold-native built for the Spark's own CPU: no -Dtarget or -Dcpu,
# about 2 s faster to start than the earlier baseline+sha2+aes build), her captured Triton kernel set (copied byte for
# byte from her recipe's image), the runner's frontend, calc.tfpc and the graph-v7-powmod bank
# (runner-assets-20261107), and her image's CUDA forward-compatibility driver.
# CUDA driver: her NGC-based image runs her engine on the CUDA 13.3 user-mode driver (libcuda 610.43.02) over the
# Sparks' 580 kernel module; on the host's 580 driver the port ran 2-7% below her at 4 and 8 streams. The image carries
# that driver's files from her image (cuda-13.3/compat/lib.real, libcuda.so.610.43.02 sha256
# 568153835562ea89c0c1669635e5631ada5f0862689025e3ed4a383086413e3a) in /opt/tensorfold/compat, and its entrypoint
# (tf-compat-entry) puts them first on the loader path only while the kernel module is older than 610 and cuInit
# succeeds through them; otherwise the host driver, as before. Each rank logs which one it uses. TF_CUDA_COMPAT=0
# forces the host driver.
ENGINE_REPO=https://github.com/jayleaton/TensorFold.git
ENGINE_REV=9c6c3d04ce34243d8ae86754a03d6c02d74fc17e
# 9c6c3d04ce34 (branch flashnext-mia-lanes) is the public twin of d306dc2fe26e: the same tree (git diff is empty),
# with one commit message reworded. Every d306dc2fe26e measurement below applies to it unchanged; the shas named in
# these notes are the builds that were measured.
# d306dc2fe26e measured on the runner image sha256:c724852087e24f456360e9150364a6a39870e55accbbd5847acc892f5c98a71f
# (native image sha256:7f3f096a854c1859e972b84929f6420c09f51383e7714b20a1e854c75d622ac8), equal layers on both nodes.
# 4c4e966eb470 measured on the runner image
# sha256:2241106de758e024666c2c1a6d95ccf0705805a01900a4edd7a8ae27cb0a6b55 (native image
# sha256:36943a849e62e80664885a436893cd873928da2b4ea85c44d703414c89fbf5b7), both labelled with the full ENGINE_REV,
# with equal layers on both nodes; its tensorfold-native has sha256
# bdd1231c3fce07055958e576f834ffe9cc273b2fa315bfaeabab45e6a955e231. (188d9c63c23a's runner image, measured below:
# sha256:af2618dca4b3273d38180341e366a012c25bf5b7a5ae3134ad79eeeccc8c42f2, tensorfold-native
# 76ce8718c1e1e8221239c10ee5ccddf73c28dc3ee2e7b1195280a601ab712890.)
IMAGE="<your-built-miatp2-9c6c3d04ce34-runner-image>"
MODEL_DIR="<absolute-qwen38-flash-next-tp2-mia-tool-full-model-directory>"
# This checkpoint's own folders: never reuse another pack's prepared files, calibration or sessions.
PREPARED_DIR="<absolute-qwen38-flash-next-tp2-mia-tool-full-prepared-directory>"
STATE_DIR="<absolute-qwen38-flash-next-tp2-mia-tool-full-state-directory>"
# Kept lane costs: mount this folder at ~/.cache/tensorfold inside each rank's container (the image runs as root; one
# folder per node and image). The engine keeps the lane scheduler's cost table in $HOME/.cache/tensorfold/window-costs,
# keyed by image, GPU, setting and environment. A rank with no table times it (about 40 s) and writes it; both ranks
# then agree on one path (kept or measured), and the boot log says which ("lanes costs (kept)" or "(measured)").
# Delete the folder to time them again.
COST_CACHE_DIR="<absolute-qwen38-flash-next-tp2-mia-tool-full-cost-cache-directory>"
HOST=localhost
PORT=8000
CHECKPOINT=nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4@fc694b54fb0174e0913e6adf86691ef85a4ead47
QUANT_FORMAT=nvfp4
CONTEXT=1048576
# Her serve flags (both ranks add --tp 2 --rank R --master <rank-0-link-address> --master-port 29551), plus a default
# thinking budget: a reply's think block closes after 8192 tokens unless the request sets thinking_budget (opencode
# sends none). On 4c4e966eb one opencode reply after a tool result ran 414 s, 21,467 tokens, all reasoning
# (2026-11-12). The budget needs d97058206 (qwen4/mia-tp2-next-budgetfix): before it, a budget cut inside a compute-lane
# result failed the reply. Booted and measured on d306dc2fe26e, 2026-11-12 (below).
SERVE_ARGS="--context 1048576 --parallel 16 --max-tokens 32768 --thinking --thinking-budget 8192 --kv-cache fp8"
TP_MASTER="<rank-0-address-on-the-link>"
TP_MASTER_PORT=29551

# Her NCCL settings: both RoCE rails, GID index 3 on both nodes, 4 channels.
NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME="<link-interface>"
NCCL_IB_HCA="<both-rail-devices-comma-separated>"
NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=3
NCCL_MIN_NCHANNELS=4
NCCL_MAX_NCHANNELS=4

# Her engine, and her m2 configuration (YaRN x4 for the 1M window, RoCE and L2 prefetch on, 16-row draft windows).
TF_FLASHNEXT_ENGINE=mia
TF_FLASHNEXT_YARN=4
TF_FLASHNEXT_ROCE=1
TF_FLASHNEXT_L2PF=1
TF_FLASHNEXT_DEPTH=15
# Her vision settings, kept as measured; the port serves text only and refuses --vision.
TENSORFOLD_MAX_IMAGES=50
TENSORFOLD_IMAGE_TOKENS=16384
TENSORFOLD_VIDEO_TOKENS=16384
TENSORFOLD_VISION_WORKSPACE_MIB=2048
TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB=10
TENSORFOLD_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1
HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1
TENSORFOLD_CUDA_KERNELS=/opt/tensorfold/share/tensorfold/cuda/sm121

# Compute runs in the engine by default, as in the TP1 candidate: every thinking chat gets the built-in tool and the
# engine runs its calls itself, whatever tools the client sends. Leave these lines as they are.
TF_COMPUTE_LANE=1
TF_COMPUTE_LANE_DEFAULT=1
# The in-model runner (the in-thinking path) on the exact circuit and graph bank, as the image ships them.
# TF_RUNNER_SPANS=reasoning (Flash-Next's default since 1a7ed13bb, stated here; her port inherits it): the runner acts
# in thinking chats only, inside the think block. A thinking-off chat gets no runner session, so no cells and no
# engine-owned values; its reply is what the engine gives with the runner off. A thinking chat's answer is the model's.
TF_RUNNER=1
TF_RUNNER_SPANS=reasoning
TF_RUNNER_CIRCUIT=/opt/tensorfold/share/runner/calc.tfpc
TF_RUNNER_FORMS=fence,repl,inline,trace
TF_RUNNER_BACKEND=graph
TF_RUNNER_GRAPH_BANK=/opt/tensorfold/share/runner/graph-v7-powmod/bank/bank.json
TF_RUNNER_STATED=0
TF_RUNNER_INLINE_CHAIN=0
# INLINE_MARK=1 (PENDING a final decision; 0 before 2026-11-12): an owned inline value ends in " @engine". Unmarked,
# Qwen kept extending a spliced big integer (7^222 by 1,600-29,700 invented digits) and once overrode the engine's right
# value with its own wrong arithmetic; marked, both stopped (measurements below). 7^222 owns 191 tokens with the mark,
# under TF_RUNNER_MAX_TOKENS (512); a marked value over the cap abstains whole and the log says so.
TF_RUNNER_INLINE_MARK=1
TF_RUNNER_SYNC_GRAPH=0
TF_RUNNER_COMPILE_STEPS=10522
TF_RUNNER_CELLS=1
TF_RUNNER_COMMIT=0
# S3: the lane's calls on the shared runner.
TF_COMPUTE_LANE_RUNNER=1
TF_COMPUTE_LANE_RUNNER_CIRCUIT=/opt/tensorfold/share/runner/calc.tfpc
TF_COMPUTE_LANE_RUNNER_BACKEND=graph
TF_COMPUTE_LANE_RUNNER_GRAPH_BANK=/opt/tensorfold/share/runner/graph-v7-powmod/bank/bank.json
TF_COMPUTE_LANE_RUNNER_SETTLE_US=3000

# Measured 2026-11-10 (22:15-23:59 UTC) on two Sparks at 2f77d333d362 with the compat driver on, one boot per arm,
# the same pack and prompts, the thermal guard on (pause 92 C). Arms: O = her original recipe image (vision off), the
# same-day control; M5 = the port plain, fresh boot; MR5 = this profile, after greedy, the arm proof, opencode and our
# speed cells.
#   Her decode protocol, tokens/s at 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 / 16 streams (her published 67.4 / - / 152.2 / - / 390.1):
#     O  69.6 / 103.1 / 156.4 / 233.2 / 372.5
#     M5 70.1 / 103.5 / 158.0 / 238.5 / 380.6   (101.0% of O at 4 streams, 102.3% at 8, 102.2% at 16)
#   Per request the port drafts as her engine does (8 streams: 133 rounds, 461 drafted; O 132, 464).
#   Heat: O peaked at 89 C; M5's rank-0 node hit 92 C in the last 4 s of its 16-stream wave (the device capped clocks
#     for those 4 s), never above it.
#   This profile (MR5): the arm proof (one modular exponentiation, greedy) made 2 lane calls, finish stop, the exact
#     answer, 0 lane warnings; opencode two-turn replay passed; check suite full 744/797 (0 leaks, as at 0811001d8).
#   This profile's protocol run, rerun 2026-11-11 00:07-00:21 UTC (each timed cell started only with both nodes at
#     or below 86 C; peaks 89 / 90 C, no pause, no clock cap): 69.0 / 100.9 / 154.7 / 233.6 / 362.6 (98.9% of O at 4
#     streams, 100.2% at 8, 97.3% at 16, against O an hour earlier). Against the port plain the runner and lane cost
#     about 6% a round at 8 and 16 streams with similar drafts (16 streams: 125.9 against 118.6 ms).
#   Excluded: its first protocol run (70.0 / 101.5 / 156.2 / 235.6 / 362.6). Its rank-1 Spark reached 94-95 C in the
#     16-stream wave and the device capped clocks for 37 s; 93 C or more lasted 10-18 s, under the 30 s stop hold.
#   Boot cost tables are stable across boots (verify 1 row: 33.2 / 33.2 ms; shared 128 rows: 121.1 / 120.4 ms).
# Earlier the same day (18:50-20:40 UTC) at 0811001d8193 on the host driver: O 69.4 / 155.1 / 237.9 / 374.9 at
#   1 / 4 / 8 / 16 streams, this profile 69.4 / 152.0 / 228.2 / 371.0; greedy replies equal 8/8 (port plain) and 7/8
#   (this profile: the in-model runner changes one); lane categories 180/180.
# Receipts: the operator archive miaport-20261110/11 (turn logs, per-arm smoke, greedy, arm proofs, speed, her
# protocol with per-round budget logs, boot cost tables, thermal logs, check-suite summaries, opencode, gate receipts;
# REPORT-miaport4.md, REPORT-miaport5.md), kept with the private engine repo's run records.
# Runner in thinking chats only, 188d9c63c23a, 2026-11-11 10:12-10:41 UTC, two Sparks, one boot per arm, the same pack,
#   the compat driver on, the cool gate on (pause 92 C): M = the same image without the runner and lane (her m2 env),
#   S = this profile's env (TF_RUNNER_SPANS then unset: the same default, the only key that differs).
#   Thinking-off replies: 0 runner cells. S's 68 consecutive thinking-off replies (our speed cells, her protocol's 32,
#     the 20-item thinking-off check set) logged no runner session, cell or closed cell; the check set's replies carry
#     no runner block. The runner still works in thinking chats: 393 cells on the check suite's lane categories.
#   Her decode protocol, tokens/s at 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 / 16 streams: M 69.8 / 101.8 / 155.7 / 232.8 / 381.8, S 69.7 / 102.6 /
#     156.8 / 237.7 / 380.6. Its 32 replies are the same text on both arms; paired per request, S decodes 1.006x M
#     (95% 1.0015-1.0108; faster on 20/32). Before 1a7ed13bb its 30 measured thinking-off replies closed 75 cells and
#     owned one value.
#   Smoke (thinking on and off, streaming equal, tool call), the arm proof (2 lane calls, exact, finish stop, 0 lane
#     warnings) and the opencode two-turn replay pass on both arms.
#   Check suite: the thinking-off set 17/20 on both arms, all 20 replies identical, no flips; lane categories 180/180
#     (MR5 and the 2026-11-10 runner arm: 179/180). One flip, a gain (arith-14). 18 of 180 replies differ from MR5,
#     all explained: 13 answers are now the model's own text where MR5's runner owned a value in the answer (the think
#     blocks are identical), and 5 arith think blocks keep the engine's forced note whole (c8e930375).
#   Engine gates: check-native-cuda-host, the host steps, fmt, lean and pr_check (0 new), gitleaks, the macOS compile
#     checks, the full suite in 2 GiB + swap (644/644 steps). The new tests fail without Flash-Next's span default.
# Computation-heavy subset on TP2 (2026-11-11, one boot, 120 tasks, frozen grader, thinking on, 4 at once,
#   270 s per request), at 2f77d333d362 with this profile's runner and lane, before c8e930375 and 1a7ed13bb:
#   92/120 (TP1's adopted R2: 93/120) at 738 tokens a task, compute used on 119 tasks (194 calls, 49 runner cells).
#   Lanes off on the same boot: 18/38 tasks started, at 6118 tokens a task.
# Computation-heavy subset on this profile as pinned (188d9c63c23a, this env), 2026-11-11 12:28-12:46 UTC, two Sparks,
#   one boot, the same driver, tasks and frozen grader as above, thinking on, the cool gate on (opened at 76 / 75 C; peak
#   88 C, no cell at or above 92 C, nothing left out):
#   92/120 at 738 tokens a task, median 12.3 s a task; all 120 started, 0 cut, 0 errors, 0 at the token limit, 0 over
#   270 s; compute used on 119 tasks (194 lane calls, 37 runner cells). Misses: no complete JSON 14, JSON type or shape
#   12, wrong answer 2. 113/120 replies are identical to the 2f77d333d run (seeded); the other 7 differ only where that
#   run's runner owned a value in the answer, which the model now writes itself, with the same grades: 92/92 there, no
#   wins or losses in any family.
#   Against TP1 (c8e930375 and 1a7ed13bb, 93/120 at 908 tokens a task, median 20.4 and 19.5 s, identical to each other):
#   won 19, lost 20 (aggregation +5/-1, division +1/-3, dp +1/-4, graph +1/-4, integer +7/-3, modular +4/-5); 19% fewer
#   tokens a task. Its thinking-off set on the same boot: 0 runner cells, 17/20, no flips, 20/20 identical to the image
#   without the runner. G was down 17 min.
# The same subset with the lanes off (2026-11-11 17:00-18:10 UTC, the same boot recipe, image and serve flags; the env
#   less its 20 TF_COMPUTE_LANE* and TF_RUNNER* keys, the other 13 keys byte for byte; same driver, tasks, frozen
#   grader, 8192-token cap, 4 at once; cool gate on, peak 90 / 88 C, no task at or above 92 C, nothing left out):
#   58/120 at 6038 tokens a task, median 141.0 s a task; all 120 started, 0 cut, 0 errors, 0 over 270 s, 0 lane calls.
#   All 58 replies that stopped are correct; the 62 misses all hit the 8192-token cap inside the reasoning, with no
#   answer. Against this profile (92/120, 738 tokens, 12.3 s): won 10, lost 44 (aggregation 20-18, division 0-16, dp
#   18-16, graph 20-16, integer 0-13, modular 0-13). Against TP1 without lanes (B: 50/120 at 6605 tokens a task,
#   median 232.4 s): won 9, lost 1. The lanes are worth +34 tasks and 8x fewer tokens a task here.
# Receipts: the operator archives mtspan-rx-20261111 (ANALYSIS.md), miaport6e (COMPUTE-COMPARE.md),
#   pincomp-rx-20261111 (ANALYSIS.md) and lanesoff-rx-20261111 (ANALYSIS.md).
# This pin, 4c4e966eb470, 2026-11-12 08:53-08:58 UTC, two Sparks, this profile's engine env byte for byte and its serve
#   flags, COST_CACHE_DIR mounted on both ranks, the compat driver on, two boots in a row (page cache not dropped):
#   Startup (rank 1's launch to rank 0 ready; rank 0 starts 16 s after rank 1): 111 s with the costs timed (an empty
#     folder), 69 s with them kept. Both ranks loaded in 47 s (weights 45-46 s) both times; timing the costs took 40 s
#     of the first boot. The table it timed (verify 1 row 33.1 ms; shared 128 rows 120.0 ms) matches 188d9c63c's boot
#     tables (33.2 ms; 121.1 / 120.4 ms), and the second boot read it back.
#   On the kept boot: smoke (thinking on and off, streaming equal, tool call) passes, the arm proof makes 2 lane calls,
#     exact, finish stop, 0 lane warnings; her decode protocol 69.97 / 155.68 / 362.16 tokens/s at 1 / 4 / 16 streams
#     (MR5 above: 69.0 / 154.7 / 362.6). The first boot's smoke passes too.
#   03ad01b69 (this pin less the two startup commits), 2026-11-12, through Mia's recipe with ENGINE=lanes: decodes at
#     0.998 of 188d9c63c's speed (paired server timings); the computation-heavy subset 92/120 at 719 tokens a task, with
#     the same tasks right and wrong as 188d9c63c. The same work is published for her recipe as engine
#     jayleaton/TensorFold flashnext-mia-lanes (52f6936c0, the same code with reworded comments).
#   Not rerun on this pin: the check suite, opencode, the thinking-off set and the computation-heavy subset under this
#     profile's own env.
#   Receipts: the operator archive bootab3 (turn log, per-arm smoke, arm proof, her protocol, both ranks' timed logs).
# This pin, d306dc2fe26e, 2026-11-12 15:17-16:01 UTC, two Sparks, this profile's env and serve flags (with
#   --thinking-budget 8192 and TF_RUNNER_INLINE_MARK=1), COST_CACHE_DIR mounted, the compat driver on (boot 79 s):
#   Smoke, arm proof (2 lane calls, exact, finish stop), toolcheck 3/3, the opencode replay, tool_choice required /
#   named / any, the budget probe 12/12 (each ran code), exact.py, lane categories 180/180, the server-log check pass.
#   Through the Spark front door with opencode: 7^222 mod 1000003 and the sum of squares 1..2026 written to a file,
#     five fresh sessions, all five exact (22-66 s each). With INLINE_MARK=0 on the same image 4 of 5 were (one
#     session distrusted the unmarked engine value 849282 and wrote its own 241549), and before the digit stop the
#     task failed on digit runaways on 4c4e966eb470 too.
#   The digit-run set (7^222; 3^300 and 2^500; 13^150; three seeds each, thinking on): 9/9 with no reasoning digit run
#     past its power's exact value (462-1,439 tokens a reply); with INLINE_MARK=0 8/9 (8 runaways in one reply, 10,402
#     tokens). 0 digit stops fired with the mark on: the mark ends the number.
#   The thinking-off set 17/20, all 20 replies byte-identical to pincomp's, 0 runner cells. The computation-heavy
#     subset 92/120 at 731 tokens a task, median 12.2 s (188d9c63c: 92/120, 738, 12.3 s); one gain, one loss; 197
#     calls, 26 runner cells (188d9c63c: 194, 37). A three-turn opencode build (a Python CLI package with tests):
#     every turn exits 0, 73 tests pass, 99 requests all 200, slowest 89 s.
#   Receipts: the operator archives jjserve5 (turn log, arm gates, digitgate json) and extgate-20261112 (swap-T1m3,
#     longoc-js5), swap-20261112/js5-rg (compute and thinking-off grades).
